{"id":"u-cf2b6675-fafb-47b1-8b5b-d84418e6eb16","src":"community","title":"Batman's Muscle Method","author":"Reyes Saúl  F.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/TGrljd-batmans-muscle-method","desc":"Unleash your inner superhero with Batman's Muscle Method, an 18-week program designed to sculpt your physique and boost your strength. With 54 intense sessions, this program focuses on athleticism and muscle building through a mix of supersets that target all major muscle groups. Expect to challenge yourself with exercises like the Romanian Deadlift and Goblet Squat, all while utilizing a full gym setup. Perfect for intermediate to advanced lifters, each 60-minute workout will push your limits and help you achieve a powerful, chiseled body. Get ready to train like the Dark Knight! \nMade: Paris Demers(the Original Creator). \n\n\nPROGRAM INSTRUCTIONS\n\n* Use the Double Progression method to progress your movements with this program. Focus on increasing reps first, then add weight once you hit the top of the rep range.\n\n* The 2-Set Structure & Failure:\n* Warm-up: Do 1 low-effort warm-up set (50-60% of your working weight) for 6–8 smooth reps to prepare your body and reduce the risk of injury. Do not fatigue the muscle.\n\n   * Working Set 1: Take this set to technical failure—the point where you can’t complete another rep with good form—and only push to full failure if you feel comfortable doing so.\n\n   * Working Set 2: If you miscalculated and your first set felt too light, immediately increase the weight for this second set to lock in absolute Mentzer-style failure.\n\n* When you see two exercises labeled as 1.a and 1.b, perform them as a superset. This means you complete all the reps for 1.a, then immediately move to 1.b without resting.\n\nOnce both are finished, rest for 2 to 3 full minutes (120–180 seconds) before starting the next round to restore your nervous system and cellular energy (ATP).\n\n Continue in this way until all prescribed sets are complete.\n\n* Drop sets are marked with *DS in your program. This means you’ll perform one drop set after your second working set. First, take your second main set to failure—the point where you can’t complete another rep with good form. Then immediately reduce the weight by about 25–40% and continue for another set until failure.\n\n* The Mentzer Tempo (4-2-4): Lower the weight over 4 seconds (eccentric), pause for 2 seconds at peak contraction or stretch to eliminate momentum, and control the ascent for 4 seconds.\n\n* Frequency: Train 3 times a week (e.g., Mon/Wed/Fri) as it fits your daily routine. If weights shoot up and you feel deeply fatigued, insert an extra rest day between sessions. Take 48-72 hours of rest between workouts. \n\n* Do the recommended warm-up before each workout to prepare your body and reduce the risk of injury.\n\n------------------------------\n🧘 WARM UP\n\n* MODERATE INTENSITY CARDIO 3 MINUTES\n* ARM CIRCLES × 30\n* WORLD’S GREATEST STRETCH × 12 / SIDE\n* DOWNWARD DOG INTO PLANK × 12","level":["Advanced","Intermediate"],"goals":["Athletics","Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":3,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-08-02T04:35:55.855Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["FULL BODY (POSTERIOR CHAIN)","FULL BODY (UPPER BODY)","FULL BODY (ANTERIOR CHAIN)"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":7,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":2}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Zercher Front-Foot Elevated Split Squat","sets":[{"lo":7,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Single Arm Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":8.5,"x":2}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Seated Hamstring Curl","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8.5,"x":2}]}]}]},{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Pull-Up (Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Goblet Squat","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":8.5,"x":2}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Incline Chest Press (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":8.5,"x":2}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":7,"hi":10,"rpe":7.5,"x":2}]},{"n":"Deficit Push Up","sets":[{"amrap":1,"rpe":8,"x":2}]}]}]},{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Hack Squat","sets":[{"lo":7,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Bent Over Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8.5,"x":2}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Dip (Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":7,"hi":10,"rpe":7.5,"x":2}]},{"n":"Single Leg Romanian Deadlift","sets":[{"lo":7,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"x":2}]}]},{"n":"Leg Extension","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8.5,"x":2}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"x":2}]}]}],[{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":7,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":2}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Zercher Front-Foot Elevated Split Squat","sets":[{"lo":7,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Single Arm Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":8.5,"x":2}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Seated Hamstring Curl","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8.5,"x":2}]}]}]},{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Pull-Up (Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Goblet Squat","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":8.5,"x":2}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Incline Chest Press (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":8.5,"x":2}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":7,"hi":10,"rpe":7.5,"x":2}]},{"n":"Deficit Push Up","sets":[{"amrap":1,"rpe":8,"x":2}]}]}]},{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Hack Squat","sets":[{"lo":7,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Bent Over Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8.5,"x":2}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Dip (Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":7,"hi":10,"rpe":7.5,"x":2}]},{"n":"Single Leg Romanian Deadlift","sets":[{"lo":7,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"x":2}]}]},{"n":"